@@ -24,6 +24,30 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Plans and billing
+
+Stripe hosts checkout and the customer portal; it posts every subscription
+change back to `/stripe/webhooks`, which is the only way subscriptions change
+in our database.
+
+| Plan | Price | Cards | Storage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free | — | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+The plans live in `app/models/subscription.rb`. The paid ones read their Stripe
+price from `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` and
+`STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`; `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and
+`STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` cover the API and the webhook signature.
+
+An account that runs out of cards keeps drafting: only publishing and creating
+cards through the API are refused.
+
+Support tools live in `/admin/accounts`: comp an account (it stops being
+billed and gets the top plan), override its card and storage limits, or reset
+the override.
+
 ## Working with Stripe
 
 The first time, you need to:
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
